EXT. HOLLOW OAK GLADE - TWILIGHT

An enormous oak, hollow as a cathedral, glows green in the dusk. Fireflies drift. A ring of toadstools circles the roots. A path of silver moss winds in from the dark.

A tiny fire burns at the center. Five travelers share it in uneasy quiet.

ODALYS THORNEWOOD-ABEBE (30s, ranger, cloak patched at the elbows) tends the flames. WILLEM "BRAMBLE" OKORO-LINDQVIST (50s, a hedge-wizard, mismatched socks) whittles a stick. MARISOL FAIRWEATHER-ODUYA (20s, a runaway princess in a stolen tunic) sits with her knees drawn up. TALIESIN ABERNATHY-KRAUSE (40s, bard, lute across his back) leans on the oak. And at the edge of the light, PIP (12, a boy thief, a sack at his belt) crouches, watching the dark.

ODALYS
We rest here till moonrise.

BRAMBLE
Aye.

MARISOL
How far?

ODALYS
Three days.

MARISOL
You said two yesterday.

ODALYS
I said two if the bridge held.

MARISOL
Did it?

ODALYS
It did not.

She stirs the fire. Sparks climb. Bramble tosses a shaving into the flames. Taliesin plucks a single string. It rings, bright, then fades.

TALIESIN
(to the glade)
Friends, a song?

BRAMBLE
No.

TALIESIN
A short one.

BRAMBLE
Short, then.

Taliesin tunes, lifts his chin, and begins to hum. Pip edges closer. Marisol rests her chin on her knees. The fire pops. For a moment the clearing is warm, almost safe.

Then the fireflies go out. All at once. The glade falls dark. The hum dies in Taliesin's throat.

PIP
(whispering)
They've gone.

ODALYS
Silence.

BRAMBLE
(muttering)
Not again.

A cold wind winds through the oak's hollow. A low voice, many voices, rises from the roots. Marisol grabs Pip's sleeve. Odalys draws her knife. Bramble raises his hands, palms out, mouth working on an unspoken word. Taliesin swings the lute off his back and holds it like a shield.

They scatter in five directions, each diving for the shadows, each convinced the others are right behind them.

The fire gutters, almost out. A single ember glows red, like an eye.
